{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he believed in YHWH.</b> He believed the content of the tidings, that the matter is settled before Elohim." "<b>And He counted it to him for righteousness.</b> Abraham counted it to the Holy One, blessed be He, as <b>righteousness</b> — for the Supreme Being will do this by His own righteousness, not by Abraham's merit. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory." "<b>And it is possible</b> to interpret <b>and He counted it to him</b>: the Holy One, blessed be He, counted the faith to Abraham in thought, as though he had performed <b>righteousness</b> in deed."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:26.111972380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}